## Settled Direction

- Inventory capability families, ownership layers, and disposition rather than optimizing raw
  script count. Narrow guarded entry points may remain when they make safety boundaries clearer.
- Introduce one pure read-side project projection contract. It resolves authority once and returns
  the executive summary and exhaustive lifecycle inventory from the same canonical interpretation.
- Keep dashboard wire formats compatible while routing its state and inventory through the shared
  projection. Retain temporary private wrappers only as compatibility shims for existing callers.
- Treat runtime-code growth as a budget: a new feature must reuse, replace, or retire an overlapping
  surface, or explicitly justify and test a net-new capability.
- Protect identity, authority, lifecycle, outcomes, planning order, closure, privacy, recovery,
  stale-state refusal, and provider portability. This is incremental convergence, not a rewrite.
- Keep the operator-facing 100k document and workflow in IDEA-0028. This map supplies its canonical
  input contract and records the surfaces it must replace or absorb.

